    "probe_text": "Done \u2014 I read the endpoint YAML (`owners.POST.yml`) and every function class in its pipeline. Here is the complete ordered list of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, exactly as the code stands.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request never enters the pipeline (`AuthorizationDeniedException` \u2192 403).\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields` (`validate`)\nBinds the request body once, then in this order:\n1. **`firstName` required** \u2014 non-blank, else `firstName` error.\n2. **`lastName` required** \u2014 non-blank, else `lastName` error.\n3. **Address normalization + required** \u2014 normalizes via `AddressNormalizer` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`/`RD\u2192ROAD`/`AVE\u2192AVENUE`); if the result is empty adds `address` error, **otherwise writes the normalized address back onto the request** (side-effect).\n4. **`city` required** \u2014 non-blank, else `city` error.\n5. **`telephone` required** \u2014 non-blank, else `telephone` error.\n6. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** \u2014 normalizes (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep `+CC`, else assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`); must be 8\u201315 digits, with national-length rule for `+61` (9) and `+1` (10); invalid adds `telephone` error, valid **writes the E.164 value back** (side-effect).\n7. **Email (optional)** \u2014 if present must match the syntactic regex; invalid adds `email` error, valid **rewrites it lower-cased** (side-effect). Absent/blank is accepted.\n8. **Postcode (optional)** \u2014 if present must be exactly 4 digits; for a known city (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in range; otherwise any 4-digit value passes. Violations add `postcode` error.\n\nAny accumulated errors throw `OwnerFieldsValidationException` \u2192 **400** with an `errors` array. Otherwise the (mutated) request is published for later steps.\n\n*Everything below runs inside a single write transaction that commits once at the end.*\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 `CheckIdentityUnique`\nDuplicate check: scans all owners; rejects with `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409** if an existing owner has **the same normalized telephone AND the same lower-cased email**. (Same-household owners with different phones are allowed.)\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 `CheckCityCapacity`\nCounts owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if **\u2265 50** \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 `BuildOwner`\nMaps the request DTO to a new `Owner` entity (`id`, `pets`, `customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `householdMemberCount` are ignored/left unset here).\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `DefaultRegistrationDate` (side-effect)\nIf no date supplied, uses the server's current date; then rolls a Saturday/Sunday forward to the next Monday. Mutates the entity's `registrationDate`.\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `CheckDailyLimit`\nCounts persisted owners with the same (adjusted) `registrationDate`; if **\u2265 100** \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode` (side-effect)\nSets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where `NNNN` = (same-city owner count) + 1.\n\n## Step 8 \u2014 `AssignHouseholdId` (side-effect)\nSets `householdId` = first 12 upper-cased hex chars of SHA-256 of `<normalized lastName>|<normalized address>`.\n\n## Step 9 \u2014 `AssignHouseholdMemberCount` (side-effect)\nSets `householdMemberCount` = (persisted owners sharing this `householdId`) + 1.\n\n## Step 10 \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount` (side-effect)\nSets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## Step 11 \u2014 `AssignBulkSignupWarning` (side-effect)\nSets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if **> 80** owners already registered on that `registrationDate`.\n\n## Step 12 \u2014 `SaveOwner` (side-effect)\nPersists the owner via `ownerRepository.save` (generates the id).\n\n## Step 13 \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated` (side-effect)\nLogs an `AUDIT` line: `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and derived `membershipLevel`.\n\n## Step 14 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\nResponds **201 Created**, `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, body = `OwnerDto` (which additionally derives response-only fields such as `membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`, `identityKey`, `contactPreference`, `locality`). The transaction commits.\n\n---\n\n**Two notes on the code as written, not the docs:**\n- The `checkIdentityUnique` step's *documented* intent (per the YAML comment and class Javadoc) is to reject on the whole derived `identityKey` `telephone|email|householdId`. The actual `service` method only compares **telephone + email** \u2014 `householdId` is computed solely to build the exception message, not to gate the match. So the effective duplicate rule is telephone+email, matching what I listed.\n- The `bulkSignupWarning` threshold (`> 80`) counts owners *before* this one is saved, while `checkDailyLimit` (`\u2265 100`) runs earlier in the same pass \u2014 both scan `findAll()` each time."
